From: Sebastien Taylor <sebastien@au-zone.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: imx95-verdin: grow npu-dma pool to 512 MiB

The Neutron NPU on Verdin i.MX95 is bound to a dedicated `npu-dma`
reserved-memory CMA pool (via `memory-region = <&npu_dma>` on the
&neutron node). The default 128 MiB is too small for larger models /
multiple concurrent inference buffers. Bump it to 512 MiB; the module
has 8 GiB of RAM so the extra CMA is well within budget and keeps the
GPU's 960 MiB `linux,cma` pool isolated from NPU allocations.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Toradex Verdin iMX95 board customization]

Signed-off-by: Sebastien Taylor <sebastien@au-zone.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95-verdin.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95-verdin.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95-verdin.dtsi
index f7d7075fec81..90b376026d73 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95-verdin.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95-verdin.dtsi
@@ -175,7 +175,7 @@ m7_reserved: memory@80000000 {

 		npu_dma: npu-dma {
 			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
-			size = <0x0 0x8000000>;
+			size = <0x0 0x20000000>;
 			alignment = <0x0 0x100000>;
 			reusable;
 		};
